Permission allow rule (../../../.claude/settings.json): Write(.claude/**) is not matched by file permission checks — only Edit(path) rules are. Use Edit(.claude/**) instead (Edit rules cover all file-editing tools).
Standards consulted: `references/a11y.md`, `form.md`, `life.md`, `api.md`.

The bug is exactly `CS-A11Y-001`: the invalid state is keyed on `error` (one *cause* of invalidity) rather than on the authoritative `validity`, so a required-and-empty group (`valueMissing`) exposes nothing to AT — and `changedProperties.has('error')` never runs when only `validity` moves.

**Single predicate** (per `CS-A11Y-001`, and `CS-A11Y-002` — one predicate, not one inlined per call site):

```js
get isInvalid() {
  return this.validity !== undefined && this.validity !== 'valid';
}
```

**`updated()`** — key the child mirroring on `isInvalid`, and react to `validity` as well as `error`:

```js
  updated(changedProperties) {
    if (changedProperties.has('error') || changedProperties.has('validity')) {
      // mirror the invalid state onto each child, from authoritative validity
      this.items.forEach((el) => {
        if (this.isInvalid) el.setAttribute('error', '');
        else el.removeAttribute('error');
      });
    }
  }
```

**`render()`** — bind `aria-invalid` declaratively, on the element that carries the `role` (the `<fieldset>`, not the host), and wire the message as the group's description so it is read on focus as well as on change:

```js
  render() {
    return html`
      <fieldset
        role="radiogroup"
        aria-invalid="${this.isInvalid ? 'true' : 'false'}"
        aria-describedby="${this.error ? 'error-message' : nothing}"
        aria-required="${this.required ? 'true' : nothing}">
        <legend><slot name="legend"></slot></legend>
        <slot></slot>
        ${this.error
          ? html`<p id="error-message" role="alert">${this.error}</p>`
          : nothing}
      </fieldset>
    `;
  }
```

Notes on the deltas:

- `role="radiogroup"` is kept deliberately — a bare `<fieldset>` is implicitly `group`, which does **not** support `aria-invalid` under ARIA 1.2; `radiogroup` does (`CS-A11Y-003`). Verify with axe rather than trusting the mapping.
- `aria-invalid="false"` is emitted explicitly rather than dropped, so the state transition is announced rather than silently disappearing.
- `aria-live="assertive"` is removed: `role="alert"` already implies an assertive live region, and doubling them causes duplicate announcements in some SR/browser pairs.
- `aria-describedby` covers the case a user focuses the group *after* the error rendered — the live region only fires on the change itself.
- `valueMissing` now surfaces even with no `error` string set. If you want it spoken and not just exposed as state, the group needs a default message for that branch — flagging rather than inventing copy.

Two follow-ups this change implies, outside the code you asked for: `CS-A11Y-002` says to check the sibling group components for the same shape (checkbox-group is the usual carrier), and `references/test.md` would want a regression test asserting `aria-invalid="true"` on the `radiogroup` for a required-and-empty group with **no** `error` set — that's the assertion the original bug would have failed.
